#
# Tracking policy (decided 2026-08-24, applied 2026-08-26)
#
# The baseline is NOT advanced just because upstream moved: a moving target
# during the first implementation of the protocol layer costs more than it buys,
# and the vectors in this suite were derived against a specific snapshot. Only a
# normative change - one of the SPEC_FILES above - interrupts development, and
# drift-check.sh exits non-zero so a scheduled CI job can open an issue.
#
# The steady state is therefore: upstream ahead, drift-check reporting the
# distance and passing.
#
# The 2026-08-26 advance is what that policy asks for on a normative change: read
# the diff, decide whether it reaches the wire, and only then move the pin. It
# reached two constants and no bytes, so moving the pin cost a rebuild of the
# host-side oracle and a one-line transcription fix. Had it reached the wire, the
# answer would have been to hold the pin and schedule the work.
#
# Revisit on the next normative change.
#
# When advancing the baseline: run scripts/drift-check.sh first, then update this
# file, then re-run scripts/verify-vectors.py and scripts/smoke-local.sh.
